15270</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Gore</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mollinger</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Shoulder motion and muscle strength of normal men and women in two age groups</article-title><source>Clin Orthop Relat Res</source><year>1985</year><fpage>268</fpage><lpage>273</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3967432</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Fyfe</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Heward</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ranges of movement at the shoulder complex using an electromagnetic movement sensor</article-title><source>Ann Rheum Dis</source><year>1991</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>824</fpage><lpage>827</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1772301</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/ard.50.11.824</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Getahun</surname><given-names>TY</given-names></name><name><surname>MacDermid</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Patterson</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Concurrent validity of patient rating scales in assessment of outcome after rotator cuff repair</article-title><source>Journal of Musculoskeletal Research</source><year>2000</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1142/S021895770000015X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group p